    <encodingDesc>
      <p>Raw CATMuS and Medusa Unicode retained separately. Same actual page pixels and segment geometry verified. Interpretation proposed, not a diplomatic ground truth. Ten reused pilot pages retain selected main zones; new pages use native unmasked full images. Detection completeness, reading order, marginalia and diagram structure require visual review. No fabricated word boxes or confidence.</p>
    <p>Stable page identifiers follow source scan filenames, not a reconciled manuscript foliation. Visible written numbers differ at several checked leaves (for example scan87r bears88, scan164r bears165). A +1 shift after the uncut83/84 bifolium is a working inference, not an exhaustively verified renumbering. Catalogue msDesc is preserved separately; see ../foliation-review.json. No source file is renamed.</p><p>Web derivative. Graphic URI resolves to the tiled viewer, not a standalone bitmap or the archival TIFF. Geometry uses pixels of the full unmasked oriented coordinate PNG, identified with its SHA256 and TIFF-to-coordinate pixel-edge affine in the corresponding page.json. Model input masks are recorded separately. Source readings and zones are unchanged. This document is an index and working data, not a complete scholarly edition.</p><p>Coordinate raster vkol-m-i-259_16v_coordinate; PNG SHA256 8ea099de092aafda4f971c2102537624a9950fedc228ad5e71df08838b5cebf5; archival TIFF SHA256 fa2a5b3afe39ea265aea543602fc23ba9eafb994fe7940d9b2b1897a3641e3f2; TIFF frame 0; counterclockwise rotation 0 degrees; TIFF-to-coordinate pixel-edge homogeneous matrix [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0], [0, 0, 1]]. These are not the coordinates of the unrotated TIFF; archival ALTO remains in TIFF coordinates.</p></encodingDesc>
